 ### FXAA (Fast Approximate Antialiasing)
-An antialiasing method that operates on the final color buffer. It performs edge detection and applies perceptually correct edge filtering. It provides antialiasing for both geometry and volume in the composited image [S5]. FXAA is applied to the final composited image, whereas multisampled G-buffer antialiasing is applied during geometry rendering. They can be combined for improved quality [S5].
