 ## Background
-The concept of filtering in volume rendering has evolved alongside hardware capabilities. Early methods relied on simple box filters for crisp edges in high-resolution volumes, while Gaussian filters were introduced to prevent banding artifacts [S1]. More recent developments include adaptive prefiltering for participating media to handle singularity artifacts [2928-prefiltering.md] and screen-space bilateral filters for preserving edges in post-processing [8374-pseudoseparable-cross-bilateral-filter.md].
